<type>(<scope>): <short description in present tense> [patch/minor/major]

# --- Common Types ---
# feat: A new feature or capability.
# fix: A bug fix.
# refactor: Rewriting code without changing its external behavior.
# test: Adding or updating tests.
# docs: Changes to documentation or README.
# chore: Maintenance tasks (updating dependencies, .gitignore, configs).

# --- Concrete Examples ---
# feat(collector): add async p2p order book fetcher [minor]
# fix(orderbook): handle missing price fields in api response [patch]
# test(pricing): add unit tests for dynamic spread calculation
# refactor(engine): split risk checks into standalone validator

# --- SemVer Pipeline Automation Guide ---
# Append one of these keywords to your header line to trigger version bumping:
#   [patch] -> Backward-compatible bug fixes (e.g., 0.1.0 -> 0.1.1)
#   [minor] -> Backward-compatible new features (e.g., 0.1.0 -> 0.2.0)
#   [major] -> Breaking changes / API overhauls (e.g., 0.1.0 -> 1.0.0)
# Leaving keywords out skips the automated version bump completely.

# [optional body: explain why the change was made]

# [optional footer: issue references, breaking changes]
